up and actions. The black plastic crate sits on a wooden table. The orange inflatable basketball is released over the black plastic crate.\n# PixelWorld generation contract v2\n\n- Use only `first_frame.png` and `prompt.txt`. Work inside this workspace. No network, other cases, reference continuations, masks, scores, memory, external AI models, learned weights, external simulation/rendering engines, or subagents.\n- Generate 20 RGB frames at 256×144, 4 fps, for 5 seconds. Frame 00 must be pixel-identical to `first_frame.png`.\n- You must create `generate.py`, run it, and call `artifact_io.save(frames, case_dir)` at least once before finishing. Finish only after the required output artifacts exist. Keep `generate.py` runnable so it regenerates the submitted RGB video.\n- Local Python drawing, image operations, shading, analytic geometry and mathematical dynamics are allowed.\n- Choose your own approach and use the tools permitted by your Track. If you revise the video, save each revised candidate before continuing. Avoid repeated revision without a clear expected improvement; aim for high-quality output while considering efficiency.\n- Use `.tmp/` for temporary files. No additional planning or method report is required.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"},{"kind":"command_execution","utc":"2026-11-11T18:33:41.773506+00:00","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat artifact_io.py && cat player_template.html'","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Output-only helpers. No drawing or generation policy is implemented here.\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport base64\nimport json\nimport wave\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n\n\ndef save(frames, case_dir, audio=None):\n    case_dir = Path(case_dir)\n    frames = np.asarray(frames)\n    path = case_dir / \"task_spec.json\"\n    spec = json.loads(path.read_text()) if path.is_file() else {}\n    n, h, w, fps = (spec.get(\"frames\", 20), spec.get(\"height\", 144), spec.get(\"width\", 256), spec.get(\"fps\", 4))\n    assert frames.shape == (n, h, w, 3) and frames.dtype == np.uint8, frames.shape\n    audio_spec = spec.get(\"audio\")\n    audio_url = None\n    if audio_spec:\n        samples = round(n / fps * audio_spec[\"sample_rate\"])\n        pcm = np.asarray(audio)\n        if pcm.ndim == 1:\n            pcm = pcm[:, None]\n        assert pcm.shape == (samples, audio_spec[\"channels\"]) and pcm.dtype == np.int16, (pcm.shape, pcm.dtype)\n        with wave.open(str(case_dir / \"audio.wav\"), \"wb\") as handle:\n            handle.setnchannels(audio_spec[\"channels\"])\n            handle.setsampwidth(2)\n            handle.setframerate(audio_spec[\"sample_rate\"])\n            handle.writeframes(pcm.astype(\"<i2\").tobytes())\n        audio_url = \"data:audio/wav;base64,\" + base64.b64encode((case_dir / \"audio.wav\").read_bytes()).decode()\n    values = frames.astype(np.uint32)\n    packed = (values[:, :, :, 0] << 16) | (values[:, :, :, 1] << 8) | values[:, :, :, 2]\n    tensor = packed.transpose(1, 2, 0)\n    np.savez_compressed(case_dir / \"pixels.npz\", pixels=tensor)\n\n    folder = case_dir / \"frames\"\n    folder.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    for index, frame in enumerate(frames):\n        Image.fromarray(frame).save(folder / f\"{index:02d}.png\")\n\n    sheet = Image.new(\"RGB\", (w * 4, (h + 21) * 2), (25, 28, 35))\n    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(sheet)\n    for index, frame_index in enumerate(np.linspace(0, n - 1, 8).round().astype(int)):\n        x, y = (index % 4) * w, (index // 4) * (h + 21)\n        draw.text((x + 5, y + 3), f\"frame {frame_index:02d} · {frame_index / fps:.2f}s\", fill=\"white\")\n        sheet.paste(Image.fromarray(frames[frame_index]), (x, y + 21))\n    sheet.save(case_dir / \"inspection.png\")\n\n    transition = Image.new(\"RGB\", (w * 4, h * 2 + 21), (25, 28, 35))\n    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(transition)\n    for index, frame_index in enumerate(min(i, n-1) for i in range(4)):\n        x = index * w\n        draw.text((x + 5, 4), f\"frame {frame_index:02d}